{
  "note": "Bank holidays 2000-2011 as listed by the government of the day (DTI/BERR, directgov, Scottish Executive/Government, nidirect), captured by the Wayback Machine, with the Royal Proclamations and Northern Ireland Orders in The Gazette as the second source (docs/sources/uk-bank-holidays-2000-2011.md). Compiled 2026-10-25 for bizdays-toolkit 0.21.0. Dates are the government list; titles are as written there (normalized in the test). Where a list also showed the weekend day itself next to its substitute (DTI 2004: 25 and 26 December), the weekend day is omitted, as GOV.UK's lists omit it.",
  "principle": "The published government list is the authority; the proclamations in The Gazette verify it. Days listed by the government but not found in any proclamation are kept and recorded in knownDifferences.",
  "fieldNotes": {
    "record": "the section of docs/sources/uk-bank-holidays-2000-2011.md that holds the transcriptions for the year",
    "sources": "per division, the government list used as the authority (Web Archive URL with capture time), or a statement that none exists for the year and division",
    "knownDifferences": "days in a government list for which no proclamation was found; returned as holidays",
    "unproclaimed": "Saturday holidays in Scotland for which neither a proclamation nor a government list was found; not returned as holidays (none in 2000-2011; the field exists so that silence can be told from absence in later ranges)"
  },
  "knownDifferences": [
    {
      "division": "scotland",
      "date": "2010-01-04",
      "listedAs": "2nd January (substitute day)",
      "note": "No Royal Proclamation appoints this day: none was found in the four searches of The Gazette recorded in docs/sources/uk-bank-holidays-2000-2011.md#1-検索に使った-url (2 January 2010 was a Saturday; Schedule 1 moves only a Sunday). Confirmed by the Scottish Government in January 2014 (dracos.co.uk/wrote/bad-bank-holidays/). Kept because the government lists of the day and banks treated it as a bank holiday."
    },
    {
      "division": "scotland",
      "date": "2011-01-04",
      "listedAs": "2nd January (substitute day)",
      "note": "No Royal Proclamation appoints this day: none was found in the four searches of The Gazette (2 January 2011 was a Sunday, moved to 3 January by Schedule 1; the three proclamations of 2010 do not mention January 2011). Confirmed by the Scottish Government in January 2014. Kept for the same reason."
    },
    {
      "division": "scotland",
      "date": "2010-12-27",
      "listedAs": "Christmas Day (substitute day)",
      "note": "No Royal Proclamation appointing 27 December 2010 in Scotland was found in the four searches of The Gazette (E-26799-1 appoints 28 December only; Schedule 1 moves Christmas Day only when it is a Sunday, and 25 December 2010 was a Saturday). Not in Somerville's article; found in this collection. Kept because every government list of the day shows it as \"Christmas Day 27 December*\"."
    }
  ],
